    "background_story": "Kenna was a brilliant physicist with a passion for unraveling the mysteries of the universe. She spent most of her career studying the intricacies of black holes and dark matter. Her colleagues often joked that she had a knack for making the most complex concepts seem explainable to anyone. Kenna's gift for simplifying the obscure led to her being invited to speak at conferences and events around the world. She was particularly known for her ability to distill dense theoretical concepts into intuitive analogies, making her a beloved figure among science enthusiasts. Kenna's work on the 'Explainable Universe' project aimed to create an open-source platform for scientists to share their research in an accessible and engaging way. Her mission was to make the wonders of the universe explainable to everyone, regardless of their background or expertise.",
